Task: Add ClientResilienceExampleSuite (resilience-client example for template adopters)

Summary:
User-requested addition, discussed mid-track: order-service (this repo's reference
service) has no outbound HTTP call, so purerest's retry + circuit-breaker middleware
was dropped entirely per the Phase 1 deviation record. But since this repo's purpose
is to be copied/adapted into real generated services that WILL call other services,
outright dropping it would leave adopters to rediscover the wiring pattern from
scratch. Added a standalone, CI-verified example test instead: wraps a dummy
Client[F] (in-memory, no real network) with Resilience.middleware, with two tests -
transient failures retried to success, and the circuit breaker opening after
repeated failures - mirroring purerest's own ResilienceSuite pattern. Deliberately
NOT wired into Main.scala/OrderServiceConfig - stays example-only so the live
service's "no resilience wiring" property (Phase 1 deviation) is unchanged.

Amended spec.md's "Deviations from order-service" and tech-stack.md's "Known
Constraints" to record this as a 2026-09-29 amendment (resilience kept as a tested
example, not dropped outright). Added a README section ("Calling other services with
resilience") pointing to the test.

Files changed:
- src/test/scala/orderservice/examples/ClientResilienceExampleSuite.scala (new)
- README.md, conductor/tech-stack.md,
  conductor/tracks/pure-service-generator_20260929/spec.md

Why: Keeps the resilience pattern discoverable and verified for whoever adapts this
template, without reintroducing dead/unexercised code into the live service.

Verification: sbt scalafmtCheck test - 26/26 pass (24 existing + 2 new).
